"summary": "Last week we hosted our Housing Outlook 2026 debate; a warm thanks to everyone who attended and contributed so well. Special thanks to the great panel made up of Caroline Pillay (L&Q), Roger Arnold (Martin Arnold Ltd), Gary Powis (Strettons) and Rosie Nesbitt, experienced voices that span the housing sector who debated four key topics including 'housing targets', the 'intermediate sector', 'making regen work' and 'private sales in a weak market'. A healthy discussion was had around targets, 16 months after the government’s announcement to build 1.5M homes by 2029.",
